gpui_windows: Untrack a window while it is destroyed

The vsync thread invalidates every tracked window. A destroyed window left
that list only when the WM_GPUI_CLOSE_ONE_WINDOW posted from WM_DESTROY was
handled, so a vsync in between called RedrawWindow on a dead handle and
logged "Invalid window handle (0x80070578)", most often when a closing
dialog hands focus back to its parent. Send the message instead: the window
leaves the list during WM_DESTROY, while its handle is still valid.

The UI thread now takes the list's write lock inside DestroyWindow, so
device-lost recovery must not hold the read lock across a SendMessageW that
waits for the UI thread. It sends the recovered devices and the later
forced redraw to the platform window only, which passes each on to every
window it tracks. Windows are added and removed on that thread, so no
message reaches a window that is gone, or a reused handle.

Remove when upstream gpui_windows untracks a window before its handle is
destroyed.

